Designers should attempt to: 
• Managing and processing a large quantity of information for a high success rate of disassembly. 
• Configuring a disassembly system as a modular system; 
• Analyse the disassembly requirements;
• Design and assess the performance of the functions needed;
• Create a disassembly domain;
• Determine the cognitive robotic functions;
• List the actions, fluents, precondition, effects required for each module;
• Program the behaviours using procedure due to complex actions; and
• Connect the modules together via actions and fluents.